    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0579" n="321" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/662</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 140]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 6, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to your despatch No. 249 of
                    January 15<anchor n="1" xml:id="d473-f1"/> in regard to the payment of freight
                    and charges incurred in connection with <pb facs="0580" n="322" xml:id="pg322"/>
                    the release of American cargoes, you are informed that the Department approves
                    your course in this matter.</p>
                <p>In this connection, it may be added that the Department has no data at hand to
                    show what particular claimants have paid freights.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilbur J. Carr</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
